CAUSE 1:
========
# One cause was conflicting or unlinked blas/lapack libraries.

# To find out, run the example file using in debug mode:

'''
$ gdb --args ./stereo_kitti Vocabulary/ORBvoc.txt /media/mrt/Whale/data/kitti/07/KITTI04-12.yaml /media/mrt/Whale/data/kitti/07/
(gdb) run # run the program
(gdb) bt  # backtrace when it crashes
'''

# In this case. the error was:

Thread 1 "stereo_kitti" received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.
0x00007fffedfa16bf in dgemm_otcopy_PRESCOTT () from /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libblas.so.3

# Fix:

'''
sudo apt update
sudo apt install libblas-dev liblapack-dev
python3 -m pip uninstall numpy -y
python3 -m pip install "numpy>=1.19.5,<1.27.0" --no-binary numpy
python3 -m pip install pybind11 scipy pandas open3d
python3 -c "import numpy; numpy.show_config()"
'''

# Look for Look for BLAS/LAPACK linkage information.

